Maintainer: Simon Garnier <garnier@njit.edu>
Description: Splits data into Gaussian type clusters using the
        Cross-Entropy Clustering ('CEC') method. This method allows for
        the simultaneous use of various types of Gaussian mixture
        models, for performing the reduction of unnecessary clusters,
        and for discovering new clusters by splitting them. 'CEC' is
        based on the work of Spurek, P. and Tabor, J. (2014)
        <doi:10.1016/j.patcog.2014.03.006>.
